YAC commands, in key order. Press keys separately.
Commands depend on the radio and current mode.

a: AF Gain. Full stop increases; comma decreases.
b: Band. Full stop next; comma previous.
d: Decoders. c CW; r RTTY; a receive audio setup.
e: New frequency. Enter MHz, then Enter.
f: Filters. See the filter keys below.
h: Help. Use h inside a control for its detailed help.
i: Tone/code input. Repeat i for CTCSS, DCS normal or DCS inverted where supported. Enter a value, then follow the prompts.
l: Split/repeater setup. Repeat l to turn it off. h then Enter at the input gives help.
m: Mode. Full stop next; comma previous.
o: Offset. Repeat o for Receive, Transmit, Clear. Full stop adds 10 hertz; comma subtracts. Either movement key clears in Clear.
p: Cycle preamp stages and off.
q: Quit YAC. y confirms; n or q cancels. Inside a control or menu, q returns and keeps changes unless its help says otherwise.
r: RF Gain, or Squelch in FM. Full stop increases; comma decreases.
s: Settings. See the settings keys below.
t: Start the configured tuner. Available only with a supported tuner. Select or enable it with s t first.
u: Cycle attenuator levels and off.
v: Read attenuator, preamp, power and supported tuner status. Power is the configured setting, not measured RF output.
w: Read signal strength, frequency, mode and active FM tone/code. Repeat w for split/repeater details.
x: Antennas. Entry reads routing; repeat x changes main antenna; r changes receive input.
z: Round frequency to the nearest kilohertz.

Comma: decrease frequency by the configured step.
Full stop: increase frequency by the configured step.

Filters: press f, then:
a: Auto Notch, or supported Beat Cancel. Repeat a to toggle.
b: Noise Blanker. Repeat b to toggle; full stop/comma adjust level while On.
c: Contour. Repeat c to toggle; full stop/comma adjust frequency while On. l selects level; w selects width; c returns to frequency.
h: Filter help.
l: Low Cut. Full stop/comma adjust.
n: Manual Notch. Repeat n to toggle; full stop/comma adjust position while On; w changes width.
p: Bandwidth. Full stop/comma adjust.
q: Return to the main menu. From an adjustment, q first returns to Filters.
r: Noise Reduction. Repeat r to toggle; full stop/comma adjust level while On.
u: Upper Cut. Full stop/comma adjust.
v: Read filters currently On. Repeat v to review individual filter states.

Settings: press s, then:
a: Read current AGC. Repeat a to select the next preset; q finishes.
b: Pi speech/braille mode. Full stop next; comma previous; q applies and saves.
e: Speech Processor. Entry reads settings; e toggles; full stop/comma adjust while On. Kenwood i/o select Input/Output. n restores entry settings; q keeps changes.
h: Settings help.
m: Guided Mic Gain. Follow preparation prompts; full stop/comma adjust. PTT remains under your control.
o: Pi speech settings. r rate; v volume; p pitch; u punctuation; full stop/comma adjust; t tests; d defaults. Changes save immediately.
p: Output power. Enter whole watts, then Enter. Blank Enter or q then Enter cancels. Successful changes announce the entered value. Icom uses an estimated conversion to relative power; v reports its percentage.
q: Return to the main menu; after AGC selection, announces Done.
s: Tuning step. Enter whole hertz, then Enter.
t: Cycle supported tuner settings. Repeat t. Selecting a tuner does not start tuning.
u: Update YAC. Shows help, then checks GitHub. r reads notes; y installs; n or q returns.
v: Select supported VFO A/B or Main/Sub.
w: Pi Wi-Fi setup. Follow the prompts; h gives help where offered.

Profile selection: type a radio number, then Space to select; q cancels.
Pi-only settings require the configured Pi launcher.

Radio recovery: Radio Error and Reconnecting start a 60-second recovery period. Radio Restored resumes operation; otherwise Aborting ends YAC. Press h while waiting for recovery help.
